course: dictionary
lesson: 6392
title: Mumble and its cousins
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: To mumble is to speak quietly and not clearly, so people find it hard to understand you. It can also be a noun: a mumble is quiet, unclear speech. «Don't mumble — speak up and look at your audience», a teacher might say, because the words are lost when they are said too softly.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Kwesi's family is staying home at half-term because Dad lost his job. When Seb asks where he's going, Kwesi mumbles «dunno yet». He does not want to say much, so his answer comes out quiet and unclear. The words around it tell you why.
explain: Mumbling can also show feelings. «Jake mumbles «ta»» suggests he is shy, or does not want to make a fuss. Kieran, who teased Mads for years, mumbles «Gonna miss you, Mads» and goes red when she hugs him. His soft, unclear words show that he finds his feelings hard to say out loud.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Kwesi mutters «dunno yet»» still makes sense, because mutter is a similar word. Mutter, murmur and whisper are close to mumble, but each one has its own feel, so think about which fits best.
fact: Mumble means to speak quietly and not clearly.
fact: A mumble, as a noun, is quiet, unclear speech.
fact: «Don't mumble — speak up» means speak clearly and loudly enough for people to hear you.
fact: In stories, mumbling often shows shyness, sleepiness or guilt, as in «he mumbled an apology».
fact: Similar words include mutter, murmur and whisper, but each one has a slightly different feel.
exercise: «Don't mumble — speak up and look at your audience.» What does mumble mean here? | Sing loudly with a big smile | Read aloud from a book | Shout the answer very fast | *Speak quietly and not clearly
exercise: Kwesi mumbles «dunno yet» to Seb. What does this suggest? | He is telling a joke | He is shouting across the playground | He is very excited about his holiday plans | *He does not want to say much, or he is unsure
exercise: Which word means a similar thing to mumble? | Dance | Stamp | Giggle | *Mutter
test: Kieran mumbles «Gonna miss you, Mads» and goes red when she hugs him. Why might he mumble? | He is telling her the time | He is shouting for help | He is singing a happy song | *He feels shy about showing his feelings
test: In this lesson, what is «a mumble»? | A type of hat worn in winter | A word for a happy song | *Quiet, unclear speech | A loud shout across the field
exam: The Hatter mumbles about «the twinkling of the tea». What is he doing? | Counting coins on the table | *Speaking quietly and unclearly | Singing a loud song | Writing a letter to the King
